cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Norviq in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Norviq: Runtime security platform for LLM agent tool calls on Kubernetes"
abstract: >-
  Norviq evaluates and enforces policy on every tool call an LLM agent makes, at
  runtime, on Kubernetes. It mediates both the agent's own tool calls and the
  Model Context Protocol surface, gating MCP servers at discovery so poisoned
  tool descriptions never reach the model's context, and again at call time.
  Policy is authored as Rego over an attested identity — namespace, workload and
  agent class derived from SPIFFE and the admission webhook's owner chain rather
  than asserted by the caller — and is distributed as signed bundles. The control
  plane ships a baseline of independently settable detectors mapped to OWASP LLM
  and MITRE ATLAS.
type: software
authors:
